.nh
.TH "GF-PROVISIONING-GET-ALERT-RULE" "1" "May 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-provisioning-get-alert-rule - Gets a specific alert rule by UID


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf provisioning get-alert-rule [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Gets a specific alert rule by UID

.PP
Response schema (GetAlertRuleOK.Payload):
  annotations                                  map
  condition                                    string               REQUIRED
  data                                         array        REQUIRED
  data[].datasourceUid                         string               Grafana data source unique identifier; it should be '\fBexpr\fP\&' for a Server Side Expression operation.
  data[].model                                 object               JSON is the raw JSON query and includes the above properties as well as custom properties.
  data[].queryType                             string               QueryType is an optional identifier for the type of query.
                                                                    It can be used to distinguish different types of queries.
  data[].refId                                 string               RefID is the unique identifier of the query, set by the frontend call.
  data[].relativeTimeRange                     object
  data[].relativeTimeRange.from                number
  data[].relativeTimeRange.to                  number
  execErrState                                 string               REQUIRED
                                                                    enum: OK | Alerting | Error
  folderUID                                    string               REQUIRED
  for                                          string               REQUIRED
  id                                           number
  isPaused                                     boolean
  keep_firing_for                              string
  labels                                       map
  missingSeriesEvalsToResolve                  number
  noDataState                                  string               REQUIRED
                                                                    enum: Alerting | NoData | OK
  notification_settings                        object
  notification_settings.active_time_intervals  array        Override the times when notifications should not be muted. These must match the name of a mute time interval defined
                                                                    in the alertmanager configuration time_intervals section. All notifications will be suppressed unless they are sent
                                                                    at the time that matches any interval.
  notification_settings.group_by               array        Override the labels by which incoming alerts are grouped together. For example, multiple alerts coming in for
                                                                    cluster=A and alertname=LatencyHigh would be batched into a single group. To aggregate by all possible labels
                                                                    use the special value '...' as the sole label name.
                                                                    This effectively disables aggregation entirely, passing through all alerts as-is. This is unlikely to be what
                                                                    you want, unless you have a very low alert volume or your upstream notification system performs its own grouping.
                                                                    Must include 'alertname' and 'grafana_folder' if not using '...'.
  notification_settings.group_interval         string               Override how long to wait before sending a notification about new alerts that are added to a group of alerts for
                                                                    which an initial notification has already been sent. (Usually ~5m or more.)
  notification_settings.group_wait             string               Override how long to initially wait to send a notification for a group of alerts. Allows to wait for an
                                                                    inhibiting alert to arrive or collect more initial alerts for the same group. (Usually ~0s to few minutes.)
  notification_settings.mute_time_intervals    array        Override the times when notifications should be muted. These must match the name of a mute time interval defined
                                                                    in the alertmanager configuration time_intervals section. When muted it will not send any notifications, but
                                                                    otherwise acts normally.
  notification_settings.receiver               string               REQUIRED
                                                                    Name of the receiver to send notifications to.
  notification_settings.repeat_interval        string               Override how long to wait before sending a notification again if it has already been sent successfully for an
                                                                    alert. (Usually ~3h or more).
                                                                    Note that this parameter is implicitly bound by Alertmanager's \fB--data.retention\fR configuration flag.
                                                                    Notifications will be resent after either repeat_interval or the data retention period have passed, whichever
                                                                    occurs first. \fBrepeat_interval\fR should not be less than \fBgroup_interval\fR\&.
  orgID                                        number               REQUIRED
  provenance                                   string
  record                                       object
  record.from                                  string               REQUIRED
                                                                    Which expression node should be used as the input for the recorded metric.
  record.metric                                string               REQUIRED
                                                                    Name of the recorded metric.
  record.target_datasource_uid                 string               Which data source should be used to write the output of the recording rule, specified by UID.
  ruleGroup                                    string               REQUIRED
  title                                        string               REQUIRED
  uid                                          string
  updated                                      string


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--describe-response-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the response payload and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get-alert-rule

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the raw HTTP response body instead of the decoded payload

.PP
\fB--uid\fP=""
	Alert rule UID [required]


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


